---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Publish and subscribe to MQTT topics

Usage: rustman mqtt [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  produce  Publish messages (a kind: mqtt request, or --value flags, or the lines of a piped stdin)
  consume  Subscribe to a topic filter and print messages as they arrive
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help

Examples:
  printf '21.5\n22.0\n' | rustman mqtt produce --broker mqtt://localhost --topic sensors/room1/temp
  rustman mqtt consume --broker mqtts://broker.example --topic 'sensors/+/temp' --json
  rustman mqtt consume sensors/temps.rman.yaml --max-messages 3
